C++14 generic lambda with struct and double argument types

Was KNOWNBUG since round 152 (main() partially type-checked): the
function-pointer lowering of a closure-eligible generic lambda type-checked
the body with `signed int` for every `auto` parameter, and `pt.x` on
`const auto &pt' was reported as an error ("member operator requires
struct/union type ... got 'const signed int'").  Fixed 2026-09-23: that
placeholder body is tried silently ([temp.inst]: the template operator()'s
body is checked at instantiation).
